----ENDF/B-VII        MATERIAL 5300                               5300 1451    7
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       5300 1451    8
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               5300 1451    9
==================================================================5300 1451   10
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         5300 1451   11
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          5300 1451   12
to the ENDF-6 Format by Bob MacFarlane (Los Alamos).              5300 1451   13
==================================================================5300 1451   14
  Contents                                                        5300 1451   15
==================================================================5300 1451   16
  MF/MT    Description                                            5300 1451   17
==================================================================5300 1451   18
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       5300 1451   19
==================================================================5300 1451   20
  Warning                                                         5300 1451   21
==================================================================5300 1451   22
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 5300 1451   23
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist5300 1451   24
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  5300 1451   25
==================================================================5300 1451   26
  Definition of Data                                              5300 1451   27
==================================================================5300 1451   28
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                5300 1451   29
==================================================================5300 1451   30
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 5300 1451   31
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       5300 1451   32
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 5300 1451   33
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              5300 1451   34
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   5300 1451   35
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     5300 1451   36
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            5300 1451   37
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  5300 1451   38
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     5300 1451   39
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     5300 1451   40
   calculates these spectra.                                      5300 1451   41
==================================================================5300 1451   42
  References                                                      5300 1451   43
==================================================================5300 1451   44
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 5300 1451   45
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   5300 1451   46
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 5300 1451   47
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 5300 1451   48
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 5300 1451   49
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    5300 1451   50
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        5300 1451   51
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    5300 1451   52
                                                                  5300 1451   53
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library5300 1451   54
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   5300 1451   55
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   5300 1451   56
  of the data, etc.                                               5300 1451   57
==================================================================5300 1451   58
  History                                                         5300 1451   59
==================================================================5300 1451   60
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         5300 1451   61
 (2) October,  2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       5300 1451   62
